==English==
{{wikidata lexeme|L4114}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|usualli}}, equivalent to {{suffix|en|usual|ly<id:adverbial>}}. Broadly displaced native {{ncog|ang|ġewunelīċe}} (from which {{ncog|en|wontly}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈjuːʒʊəli/|/ˈjuːʒli/|/ˈjuːʒəli/|a=RP,US,CA}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈju.ʒu.(ə.)li/|/ˈju.ʒə.li/|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-usually.ogg|a=US}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈjʉːʒʊə.li/|a=Aus}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈjuʒ(ʊ)wəli/|a=Indic}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# {{U|most of the time}}; less than [[always]], but more than [[occasionally]].
#: {{ux|en|Except for one or two days a year, he '''usually''' walks to work.}}
#* {{RQ:Chambers Younger Set|IX|passage=He and Gerald '''usually''' challenged the rollers in a sponson canoe when Gerald was there for the weekend ; or, when Lansing came down, the two took long swims seaward or cruised about in Gerald's dory, clad in their swimming-suits; and Selwyn's youth became renewed in a manner almost ridiculous,{{nb...}}.}}
#* {{RQ:en:New York Times|date=2020-04-16|author=Patricia Cohen|title=Straggling in a Good Economy, and Now Struggling in a Crisis|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2020/04/16/business/economy/coronavirus-economy.html|passage=The coronavirus shock has made the economic precariousness — '''usually''' seen in scattershot fashion — evident everywhere at once.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20200724025144/https://www.nytimes.com/2020/04/16/business/economy/coronavirus-economy.html}}
# Under [[normal]] [[condition]]s.

